    "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11018": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Department of Counseling, Educational Leadership, and School Psychology",
      "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct, Department of Counseling, Educational Leadership, and School Psychology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct, Department of Counseling, Educational Leadership, and School Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1602/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct, Department of Counseling, Educational Leadership, and School Psychology Department Name Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Position Overview The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development ( FSEHD ) at Rhode Island College prepares educators, counselors, school psychologists, wellness and exercise science, and youth development professionals who positively impact schools, communities, and the lives of children, youth, and adults. The FSEHD is committed to excellence, equity, inclusion, community engagement, and preparing highly qualified professionals throughout Rhode Island and beyond. The FSEHD invites applications from qualified professionals interested in serving as adjunct faculty teaching content, practicum, or seminar courses and/or supervising student teachers or interns across its undergraduate and graduate programs. Essential Duties Department of Counseling, Educational Leadership, and School Psychology ( CEP ) – Programs: Clinical Mental Health Counseling School Psychology Assignments may include: Teaching undergraduate or graduate content courses. Teaching practicum, internship, or seminar courses. Serving as a college supervisor. Supervising student teachers or interns in PK-12 settings or counseling, youth development, or wellness and exercise community organizations. Contact: Shannon Dowd-Eagle or Kalina Brabeck, Co-Chairs Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Dean of the FSEHD . Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications Master’s degree. Relevant professional experience in the field. Experience working with diverse learners and communities. Strong communication, mentoring, and supervisory skills. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate Degree preferred. Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00064 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Posting Date 07/01/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
