    "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/10980": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor Operations Management",
      "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Assistant/Associate/Professor Operations Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Assistant/Associate/Professor Operations Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates who have an earned master’s degree or equivalent and are pursuing a terminal degree but who have not yet completed their terminal degree by the date of appointment may be considered for appointment at the rank of instructor. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Upon hire, candidate will be required to arrange for an official transcript of highest degree earned to be mailed/transmitted directly from the institution to RIC. Candidates will be prompted during the application process to provide 3 names and email addresses for reference letters. Position Information Position Information Posting Number F00281 Position Title Assistant/Associate/Professor Operations Management Division Academic Affairs Division Department Name School of Business Position Type Faculty Position Overview The IACBE -accredited School of Business at Rhode Island College invites applications for an open-rank, tenure-track faculty position in Operations Management. The successful candidate will teach a variety of operations and management-related courses, including operations management, project management, supply chain management, process management, service operations, and quality assurance, with possible opportunities to teach additional management courses. Essential Duties The IACBE -accredited School of Business at Rhode Island College invites applications for one open rank, tenure-track faculty position (assistant, associate, or full) with a primary focus in Operations Management. We seek candidates with a strong interest in teaching within a liberal arts setting who are eager to teach various operations management courses, including operations management, project management, supply chain management, process management, service operation management, and quality assurance. There may also be opportunities to teach other courses in the broad management area. Successful candidates will be expected to teach three courses in the fall and spring terms (3-3 load). The classes are small, allowing for more student interaction. The college has an average student-to-faculty ratio of 14:1, and most class sizes range between 10 and 30 students. Faculty are also required to advise up to 30 students, which requires guiding students through their management programs. Faculty are also expected to engage in scholarly research leading to publication in peer-reviewed journals and conduct service. The college requires that all applicants and employees be able to perform the above essential duties of the job and will explore reasonable accommodations for individuals with documented disabilities in accordance with ADA requirements. Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Department Chair. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Good teaching skills, Good knowledge of operations management (including project management, process management, service management, and supply chain management) The ability and enthusiasm to impart this knowledge to undergraduate students, A willingness to work collegially with other faculty in the School of Business Required Qualifications Ph.D. or D.B.A. in Operations Management or related field, or ABD with a credible plan to complete dissertation within 2 years. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the college level. Industry experience in an asset. Interest in teaching and researching Ability to teach in-person, hybrid, or online as directed by the chair and/or dean of the School of Business. Bilingual Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Position Details FLSA Exempt Full Time / Part Time Full-time Proposed Compensation Benefits Full-time employee benefits include: Comprehensive Health Benefits and Rewards for Wellness Incentives Generous Paid Time Off Family/Parental Leave Tuition Waivers at RIC , CCRI & URI Retirement Plan Long-term Disability Coverage Variety of voluntary add-on’s For a complete listing, visit: http://www.employeebenefits.ri.gov/benefits/new/index.php Reports to (Title) Academic or Calendar Year Academic Position Status Continuing Tenure Track End of Temporary or Limited Position Collective Bargaining Unit RIC/AFT Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Application Posting Date 09/24/2024 Application Closing Date Special Instructions Candidates who have an earned master’s degree or equivalent and are pursuing a terminal degree but who have not yet completed their terminal degree by the date of appointment may be considered for appointment at the rank of instructor. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Upon hire, candidate will be required to arrange for an official transcript of highest degree earned to be mailed/transmitted directly from the institution to RIC . Candidates will be prompted during the application process to provide 3 names and email addresses for reference letters. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you hold a Ph.D. or DBA in Operations Management or related field OR ABD with credible plan to complete dissertation within 2 years? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Writing Sample Writing Sample 2 Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
