    "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11227": {
      "title": "Legal Assistant",
      "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Legal Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Legal Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Salary range: $50 - $60 per hour. Location: On site in Providence, RI. Appointment Type: Temporary, Part-Time (approximately 19 hours/week) Duration: Up to 90–180 days (with possible extension) This position is structured as a part-time, temporary appointment (approximately 19 hours per week) Flexible or hybrid work arrangements may be considered based on candidate availability and institutional need. If remote work is approved, it must be performed within Massachusetts, Connecticut, or Rhode Island due to payroll and tax requirements. Posting Details Posting Detail Information Posting Number NT00133 Position Title/Assigment Legal Assistant Department Name Office of the President Position Type Staff - Casual Position Description Basic Functions Serve as legal assistant to the Office of the General Counsel while also providing high-level confidential administrative and operational support for executive-level institutional initiatives and matters under the direction of the President’s Office. The incumbent will provide a full range of legal and executive administrative services in a fast-paced environment and will be required to work independently, efficiently, and in a time-sensitive manner. The incumbent will be exposed to sensitive, confidential, and/or privileged information and communications which must be held in strict confidence. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Assist the General Counsel and President’s Office in carrying out professional, administrative, operational, and institutional responsibilities relating to legal services, executive initiatives, and College operations as required. Process and type legal memoranda using proper legal citations to federal and state statutes, regulations, and case law. Process and type legal documents and instruments of every kind, including by way of example and not limitation, contracts and memorandum. Assist General Counsel in the preparation, review, processing, and approval of college contracts, including previewing documents to identify contracts and contract language requiring attorney review and contracts and contract language previously approved. Assist General Counsel in the review, preparation, revision and approval process of college policies. Coordinate and manage, in consultation with the General Counsel formal responses to the Rhode Island Access to Public Records (“APRA”) requests, and communications regarding other legal notices. Complete annual Rhode Island Attorney General APRA and Open Meetings Act (“OMA”) training. Provide confidential administrative services, including the following: arrange and schedule meetings; prepare, maintain and type reports, memoranda and correspondence; draft and respond to routine correspondence; prepare and maintain spreadsheets. Maintain a high degree of professionalism and sensitivity, in dealing directly with the public, students, faculty, staff, and officials (both within and outside the College) on behalf of the General Counsel. Prioritize responses to correspondence, phone calls and various issues, thereby minimizing demands on the time of the General Counsel, allowing them to focus on broader and more critical issues. Maintain and manage computer file system; prepare and administer legal file folders and manage record retention and destruction and documentation of destruction of files in consultation with the General Counsel and in accordance with department protocols. Maintain and file state OMA and APRA training certificates and continuing legal education certificates for General Counsel and staff. In consultation with the General Counsel develop and maintain office files and budget records and ensure their confidentiality. Assist with special projects, executive initiatives, institutional communications, and operational matters on behalf of the President’s Office and Executive Team as assigned. Provide confidential administrative and coordination support related to Executive Team meetings, institutional initiatives, strategic planning efforts, and cross-divisional projects. Prepare, coordinate, track, and maintain sensitive materials, reports, presentations, and correspondence related to executive-level initiatives and institutional priorities. Coordinate communications and follow-up activities among senior leadership offices while maintaining appropriate confidentiality and professionalism. Support institutional compliance, governance, policy, and operational functions as assigned by the President’s Office and Office of the General Counsel. Other duties and responsibilities: Perform other duties as assigned. Licenses, tools and equipment: Personal computers, printers, word processing, database management, and spreadsheet software. Microsoft Office. Environmental conditions: The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Required qualifications: Associate’s Degree. Demonstrated experience in a responsible legal support position; Demonstrated organizational skills; Demonstrated ability to handle multiple assignments concurrently; Demonstrated ability to independently resolve issues under tight deadlines; Demonstrated strong verbal and interpersonal communication skills; Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills; Demonstrated attention to detail; Demonstrated experience in using Microsoft Office platform programs; and, Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Preferred qualifications: Demonstrated experience in a responsible legal support position within an institution of higher education. Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Benefits Eligible? No Application Open Date 06/29/2026 Additional Information Salary range: $50 – $60 per hour. Location: On site in Providence, RI. Appointment Type: Temporary, Part-Time (approximately 19 hours/week) Duration: Up to 90–180 days (with possible extension) This position is structured as a part-time, temporary appointment (approximately 19 hours per week) Flexible or hybrid work arrangements may be considered based on candidate availability and institutional need. If remote work is approved, it must be performed within Massachusetts, Connecticut, or Rhode Island due to payroll and tax requirements. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have an Associate's, Bachelor's, or Master's Degree? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
