      "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjuncts, Biology Department (Anatomy and Physiology) (2026) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjuncts, Biology Department (Anatomy and Physiology) (2026) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC/AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1122 (lab)-$1548 (lecture)/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjuncts, Biology Department (Anatomy and Physiology) (2026) Department Name Biology Department Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Faculty of Arts and Science Position Overview The Biology Department is seeking candidates to fill part-time instructor positions with expertise in Anatomy and Physiology. We welcome applications from those qualified to teach introductory, intermediate and advanced courses. We seek adjunct faculty committed to teaching and working with our multicultural student population, teaching courses as needed at the undergraduate/graduate level. Essential Duties Teach in-person specialty classes populated by students majoring in the following areas: Biology, Health Sciences, Nursing: this includes the new Anatomy & Physiology. Occasional Duties Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications M.A. in a biological science Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate instruction and to mentoring students Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching introductory biology and advanced courses including human anatomy and physiology. Experience with nontraditional students and with an ethnically-diverse student population Environmental Conditions Teaching/instruction is performed in a traditional classroom setting. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00052 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Fall 2026 Posting Date 05/07/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC / AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
