    "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11054": {
      "title": "Cyber-Range Operator",
      "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Cyber-Range Operator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Cyber-Range Operator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Compensation: $45 - $60 per hour Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Posting Details Posting Detail Information Posting Number NT00132 Position Title/Assigment Cyber-Range Operator Department Name Institute for Cybersecurity & Emerging Technologies Position Type Staff - Casual Position Description Primary Purpose The Cyber Range Operator supports cyber resilience for students and community partners by organizing and executing high-intensity simulated cyberattack exercises in a state-of-the-art environment. These trainings are designed to evaluate participant preparedness, response effectiveness, and operational decision-making under pressures associated with data breaches and related cyber incidents. This role focuses on structured adversarial testing, incident escalation modeling, playbook readiness, and pre-and post-exercise analysis to educated students in the intricacies of cyber-defense and improve overall enterprise security posture. Essential job functions: Learn and facilitate cyberattack simulations within a controlled physical and logical environment. Support red-team and cyber range operations to evaluate defensive capabilities. Assist instructors in the delivery of educational cyberattack scenarios to students of all skill levels. Monitor and evaluate participant performance and response effectiveness during simulated incidents. Identify gaps in technical controls, communication workflows, and escalation procedures. Document findings and provide clear, actionable recommendations to stakeholders. Contribute to the development and refinement of incident response playbooks. Ensure all activities comply with organizational policies, legal requirements, and ethical standards. Ensure cyber range software/hardware and other administrative tasks are maintained and up-to-date as needed. Work with other Institute staff to ensure Range calendar and scheduling is kept current. Occasional job functions: Attend occasional meetings, events, and conferences related to cyber-range and/or Institute for Cybersecurity & Emerging Technologies. Travel to customer sites for range-related activities. Perform other duties as assigned by the Institute director. Required qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Information Security, Computer Science, or a related field and equivalent experience/certifications Professional experience in cybersecurity operations, incident response, or threat simulation. Expert knowledge of network security, system behavior, and attack/defense methodologies. Experience in a training or instruction environment. Ability to perform effectively in time-sensitive, high-pressure scenarios. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Preferred qualifications: Industry certifications such as CISSP , CEH , OSCP , or equivalent. Experience with cyber range platforms, tabletop exercises, or red-team engagements. Familiarity with regulatory and compliance frameworks (e.g., NIST , ISO , SOC 2). Experience working in enterprise or regulated environments. Environmental conditions: The employee is not exposed to any known adverse environmental conditions. Posting Information Number of Positions Available 1 Benefits Eligible? No Application Open Date 07/06/2026 Additional Information Compensation: $45 – $60 per hour Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. EEO Statement Rhode Island College is an equal opportunity employer. The institution does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability religion, age, veteran status, or any other protected status under applicable law. Rhode Island College is committed to maintain a workplace and educational environment that supports equal opportunity, professionalism and respectful engagement for all community members. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have a Bachelor’s degree in Information Security, Computer Science, or a related field and equivalent experience/certifications? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/11023": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Department of Elementary Education",
      "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct, Department of Elementary Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct, Department of Elementary Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1602/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct, Department of Elementary Education Department Name Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Feinstein School of Education and Human Development Position Overview The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development ( FSEHD ) at Rhode Island College prepares educators, counselors, school psychologists, wellness and exercise science, and youth development professionals who positively impact schools, communities, and the lives of children, youth, and adults. The FSEHD is committed to excellence, equity, inclusion, community engagement, and preparing highly qualified professionals throughout Rhode Island and beyond. The FSEHD invites applications from qualified professionals interested in serving as adjunct faculty teaching content, practicum, or seminar courses and/or supervising student teachers or interns across its undergraduate and graduate programs. Essential Duties Department of Elementary Education – Programs: Elementary Education undergraduate Program Elementary Education MAT graduate Program Reading Specialist Program Early Childhood Undergraduate Program Early Childhood Undergraduate Certificate Program – Bilingual Spanish/English Assignments may include: Teaching undergraduate or graduate content courses. Teaching practicum, internship, or seminar courses. Serving as a college supervisor. Supervising student teachers or interns in PK-12 settings or counseling, youth development, or wellness and exercise community organizations. Contact: Karen Capraro, Chair of the Elementary Education Department Occasional Duties Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Dean of the FSEHD . Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications Master’s degree. Relevant professional experience in the field. Experience working with diverse learners and communities. Strong communication, mentoring, and supervisory skills. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate Degree preferred. Environmental Conditions The employee is not exposed to known adverse environmental conditions. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00065 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available Multiple Anticipated Start Date or Semester Posting Date 07/07/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Please be advised that the college is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as instructional and supervisory needs arise. The Feinstein School of Education and Human Development welcomes applications from individuals committed to excellence in teaching, mentoring, supervision, and professional preparation. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
