nal Duties Email communications with department Chair and other faculty Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Familiarity with a learning management system. Knowledge of marketing principles and methods. Ability to engage students in active learning. Required Qualifications Minimum of a Master’s degree in Marketing, Business Administration or related field as well as some post-secondary teaching experience with related industry experience. Preferred Qualifications A minimum of 2- year college teaching experience with industry experience in marketing. Environmental Conditions This is an in person class taught in a RIC classroom Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00053 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available 1 Anticipated Start Date or Semester Fall 2026 Posting Date 05/27/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants Candidates must have authorization to work in the US without the need for employer sponsorship. Appointment is contingent upon receipt of an acceptable background screening conducted once selected for the position. UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC / AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. Payment is made once a month; applicable taxes are withheld. There are no fringe benefits with this position. Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. Applications for these positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed if openings become available . Writing sample, teaching evaluations and/or letters of recommendation are not required at time of application and are required only if requested directly by the department chair. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have Master's degree in Marketing, Business Administration or related field as well as some post-secondary teaching experience with related industry experience? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
