    "https://employment.ric.edu/postings/10561": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Graphic Design Instructor",
      "description": "Rhode Island College Employment Opportunities | Adjunct, Graphic Design Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security Report Applicant FAQs Adjunct, Graphic Design Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. -UNION ELIGIBILITY: Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC/AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. -Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. -Candidates are required to provide digital images of personal and student work, submitted as either a .pdf file or a link. Use the Multi Media 1 button (no cds, usb drives, or hard copies.) -Candidates are required to provide a teaching statement. Use the Teaching Philosophy 1 button. -During the application process candidates will be prompted to provide names and contact information for three current references. -An optional button has been provided in case candidates wish to upload additional information. Note: Candidates having specific questions can address their inquiries to: Professor Heemong Kim, (401-456-9691 or hkim@ric.edu) Posting Details Classification Information FLSA Exempt Rate Per Credit Hour $1602/credit hour Position Information Position Title Adjunct, Graphic Design Instructor Department Name Art Department Academic or Calendar Year Academic School Name Other Position Overview This position involves teaching undergraduate BA and BFA students the core concepts and practical skills of professional Graphic Design, guiding them from introductory foundations through advanced applications. The instructor will develop and deliver coursework that builds students’ creative, conceptual, and technical abilities across key areas of the field, including typography, publication design, branding design, and package design. Essential Duties The individual will teach BA and BFA students professional Graphic Design concepts and skills from the beginning to advanced levels, such as typography, publication design, branding design, and package design. Occasional Duties Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required Qualifications MFA in Graphic Design or comparable and significant professional experience or four-year degree and extensive professional experience. Preferred Qualifications College teaching experience. Environmental Conditions Graphic Design studio courses are taught in a Macintosh computer lab and are capped at 15 students. An adjacent seminar is available on select days/times. This facility includes a projector with a sound system, worktables, inkjet and color laser printers, paper cutters, a light box, book binding tools, a selection of other small tools for building projects, flat files, a ventilated spray room, a large storage closet, and cupboards. Floor-to-ceiling windows are equipped with blackout blinds. All graphic design students have access to open lab hours on select days. There is a shared adjunct office on the first floor of the Art Center. Posting Detail Information Posting Number A00059 Benefits Eligible? No Number of Positions Available 1 Anticipated Start Date or Semester Posting Date 03/10/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions/Information for Applicants - UNION ELIGIBILITY : Adjuncts become eligible to join the RIC / AFT Adjunct Union if they complete 6 load hours (excludes applied music) within the two previous consecutive years. -Upon hire, candidate will be required to provide an official transcript of highest degree earned. -Candidates are required to provide digital images of personal and student work, submitted as either a .pdf file or a link. Use the Multi Media 1 button (no cds, usb drives, or hard copies.) -Candidates are required to provide a teaching statement. Use the Teaching Philosophy 1 button. -During the application process candidates will be prompted to provide names and contact information for three current references. -An optional button has been provided in case candidates wish to upload additional information. Note: Candidates having specific questions can address their inquiries to: Professor Heemong Kim, (401-456-9691 or hkim@ric.edu) Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Multi Media Optional Documents Rhode Island College 600 Mount Pleasant Avenue Providence, RI 02908 (401) 456-8216 www.ric.edu RIC is an EEO/E-Verify Employer To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
